Q: Show a simple Quarkus REST + service + DB style implementation (Spring-like layers)

Think Spring Boot structure, Quarkus annotations.

────────────────────────────────────────
1) Entity (Panache Active Record style)

@Entity
public class User extends PanacheEntity {
    public String name;
    public String email;
}

// PanacheEntity gives you id + helpers: listAll(), findById(), persist()...

────────────────────────────────────────
2) Service (CDI bean)

@ApplicationScoped
public class UserService {

    public List<User> findAll() {
        return User.listAll();
    }

    @Transactional
    public User create(String name, String email) {
        User u = new User();
        u.name = name;
        u.email = email;
        u.persist();
        return u;
    }

    public User find(Long id) {
        return User.findById(id);
    }
}

────────────────────────────────────────
3) REST resource (≈ @RestController)

@Path("/users")
@Produces(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON)
@Consumes(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON)
public class UserResource {

    @Inject
    UserService userService;

    @GET
    public List<User> all() {
        return userService.findAll();
    }

    @GET
    @Path("/{id}")
    public User byId(@PathParam("id") Long id) {
        User u = userService.find(id);
        if (u == null) {
            throw new NotFoundException();
        }
        return u;
    }

    @POST
    public Response create(User request) {
        User saved = userService.create(request.name, request.email);
        return Response.status(Response.Status.CREATED).entity(saved).build();
    }
}

────────────────────────────────────────
4) Config (application.properties)

quarkus.datasource.db-kind=postgresql
quarkus.datasource.username=app
quarkus.datasource.password=secret
quarkus.datasource.jdbc.url=jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/app
quarkus.hibernate-orm.database.generation=update

# HTTP
quarkus.http.port=8080

────────────────────────────────────────
5) Run

./mvnw quarkus:dev
# live reload Dev Mode

Native (concept):
./mvnw package -Dnative

────────────────────────────────────────
Spring mapping of this example

| This Quarkus piece     | Spring Boot equivalent        |
| ---------------------- | ----------------------------- |
| `@Path` resource       | `@RestController`             |
| `@Inject`              | constructor/`@Autowired`      |
| `@ApplicationScoped`   | `@Service`                    |
| `PanacheEntity`        | Entity + JpaRepository        |
| `quarkus:dev`          | bootRun + optional DevTools   |

